From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:45:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView+WebContent: Let the embedder run a script in a
 document now

A browser's extensions run scripts in a tab's frames when they ask, not
only at document start, end, or idle, and want each frame's result back,
as chrome.scripting.executeScript() does.

ScriptBridgeEndpoint::run_user_script() runs a Web::HTML::UserScript in
the endpoint's document, in the world the script names, once the
document reaches the script's injection time. It answers with the
script's completion value as JSON, once the value settles if it's a
promise, or with nothing for undefined, an exception, or a rejection. It
answers that the script didn't run if the document has gone, or is no
longer its navigable's active document. A script that takes a bridge
gives its world one, as at document start.

ViewImplementation::frame_document_endpoints() lists the documents in a
view's frames, wherever site isolation hosts them, for the embedder to
choose from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
